# ==========================================
# Domain Boundaries
# ==========================================

- NEVER access another domain's Repository directly.
- A Service may only use Repositories that belong to its own domain.
- Cross-domain communication MUST happen through the corresponding Service.
- The only allowed exception is read-only access to UserRepository for public profile data (username, avatar, displayName).

Examples:

✔ MessageService -> NotificationService
✔ FollowService -> UserRepository (public profile only)

✘ MessageService -> NotificationRepository
✘ PostService -> FollowRepository


# ==========================================
# Authorization
# ==========================================

- Every Repository query that returns data visible to another user MUST receive viewerId (or currentUserId) explicitly.
- Visibility and ownership filtering MUST be enforced inside the SQL/JPA query.
- NEVER filter permissions only inside the Service layer.

Correct example:

findVisiblePostsByAuthor(
    UUID authorId,
    UUID viewerId,
    Instant cursor,
    UUID cursorId,
    int limit
)

Incorrect example:

findPostsByAuthor(UUID authorId)


# ==========================================
# Ownership Validation
# ==========================================

- Every UPDATE or DELETE on user-owned resources MUST verify ownership in the database query itself.
- NEVER perform ownership validation only before executing the update.

Correct example:

UPDATE posts
SET content = :content
WHERE id = :id
AND author_id = :currentUserId

Incorrect example:

SELECT post
IF owner
UPDATE posts...


# ==========================================
# Counters
# ==========================================

- Persistent counters live ONLY in PostgreSQL.
- Counters MUST be updated using atomic UPDATE statements.
- Redis MUST NOT store persistent counters.

Redis is allowed only for:

- unread notifications
- rate limiting
- temporary cache
- session-related data

Redis MUST NOT store:

- likeCount
- followerCount
- followingCount
- commentCount


# ==========================================
# Cursor Pagination
# ==========================================

- Cursor pagination MUST always use a composite cursor.

Cursor:

(createdAt, id)

Ordering:

ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC

NEVER paginate only by timestamp.


# ==========================================
# Testing
# ==========================================

- A feature is NOT considered complete without integration tests.
- Integration tests MUST use Testcontainers.
- Every protected endpoint MUST include at least one authorization isolation test.

Minimum required scenarios:

✔ owner access
✔ unauthorized access
✔ authenticated access from another user
✔ resource not found


# ==========================================
# Repository Design
# ==========================================

- Repository methods MUST enforce visibility rules.
- Repository methods MUST never return unauthorized entities.
- Business rules remain in Services.
- Ownership and visibility constraints belong to Repository queries.


# ==========================================
# Architecture
# ==========================================

- Services communicate only with Services.
- Controllers communicate only with Services.
- Repositories communicate only with the database.
- Controllers MUST NEVER access Repositories directly.
- Services MUST NEVER access Controllers.

# ==========================================
# Code Style
# ==========================================

- Use Lombok annotations (@Getter, @Setter, @Builder) instead of manual boilerplate.
- Entity classes use @PrePersist/@PreUpdate for UUID generation and timestamps, never database defaults.
- DTOs are Java records, never classes with mutable setters.
- Never expose entity classes directly in Controller responses; always map to a Response DTO.

# ==========================================
# Database Migrations
# ==========================================

- Every schema change requires a new Flyway migration file: V{n}__description.sql.
- NEVER modify an existing migration file after it has been committed.
- ddl-auto is always "validate", never "update" or "create"

# ==========================================
# Circular Dependencies
# ==========================================

- Circular Service dependencies resolved via @Lazy are tolerated only when
  refactoring into three separate Services would break domain isolation.
- Before introducing @Lazy, evaluate whether the shared responsibility should
  be extracted into a new, smaller Service.

# ==========================================
# Commits
# ==========================================

- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, refactor:, test:, docs:.
- Each commit corresponds to one phase or one correction item, never multiple unrelated changes.